      "message": "Nit: Maybe this is a broader comment on the way that this task stores command responses, but this seems like an odd thing to cache in the task state. It could change at any time without notification from the PDC. Right now, it\u0027s only being read immediately after setting it with the command response. But it would make a little more sense to me to structure the command/response code so that it works with some structure specific to that command process, and the result would only be stored in `pdc_port_t` if the value was expected to be durable.",
